    fix(graph): wire a real similar-class edge producer (OB-GAP-067)
    
    problem_edges was permanently empty: Store.CreateEdge had no production
    caller, so GET /api/v1/problems/<class>/related answered {"related":[]} and
    POST .../discover returned an empty related list on a fully seeded database,
    while README, docs/integration.md, docs/api-reference.md and the OpenAPI spec
    all documented traversal as working.
    
    - graph: accept the documented `similar` relationship (EdgeSimilar) in the
      CreateEdge switch. docs/integration.md and docs/api-reference.md have always
      shown that value; only the store rejected it.
    - graph/linker.go (new): deterministic, provenance-honest title-lexeme linker.
      TitleTokens lowercases, splits on non-alphanumeric runs, drops tokens
      shorter than 3 chars and the six-word stopword set, and dedupes.
      LinkSimilarClasses(classID, minShared, maxNeighbors) loads the class, scores
      every other class by |A n B| / min(|A|,|B|) clamped to (0,1], keeps the top
      maxNeighbors by weight (tiebreak: shared desc, then title asc) and writes
      `similar` edges BOTH ways, ignoring ErrDuplicate so it is idempotent.
      LinkAllSimilar runs it across every class.
      Why titles: the corpus carries no error signature (answers[].signatures is
      solve metadata: {model,result,tests,problem_class}), so the class title slug
      is the only relationship signal the data actually has. Why both directions:
      every traversal read here (ListEdgesFrom, relatedClasses, Discovery, the
      /related handler) is single-directional, so a one-sided write would make
      /problems/A/related list B while /problems/B/related stayed empty. Why
      `similar`: shared words are evidence of family resemblance, not proof of a
      shared root cause.
    - seed: link the whole corpus after the file loop (LinkAllSimilar(ctx, 2, 5));
      Stats gains EdgesCreated, 0 on a re-run.
    - import: importAnswer links the class it just added or updated, best-effort —
      a linker failure can never turn an already-committed import into a reported
      failure. ImportResult gains EdgesCreated (internal; the /import wire shape
      is built by the handler and is unchanged).
    
    Live evidence on a scratch DB (the live DB and service were never touched):
      off-by-one seed -dir .../data -db /tmp/oby382/scratch.db
        -> files=1793; classes=1793 created / 0 existing; answers=1880 created;
           edges=7004 created
      second run -> edges=0 created, problem_edges stays 7004 (idempotent)
      GET http://127.0.0.1:8771/api/v1/problems/python-sdk-idle-audit/related
        -> non-empty related[] with problem_class/relationship/weight:
           h3-sdk-python-idle-audit-tick 1, idle-audit-python-sdk 1,
           python-idle-audit 1, go-idle-audit 1,
           python-sdk-duckdb-board-audit 0.75, h3-sdk-idle-audit-tick 0.75
      (so-nil-pointer-deref has no token-mates in this corpus, so a class that
       does was used for the probe.)
    
    Tests: graph.TestLinkSimilarClassesCreatesEdges / RespectsMinShared /
    RejectsZeroID / TestTitleTokens, seed.TestSeedCreatesRelatedEdges,
    import.TestImportLinksSimilarEdges. RED-proved by reverting each producer in
    turn: removing the CreateEdge case fails with
    `create similar edge 1->2: invalid relationship "similar"`; removing the seed
    call fails with `Seed stats EdgesCreated = 0, want > 0`; removing the link call
    on the added path fails with `edges created = 0, want 2`.
    
